VERDICT: REPAIR
I completed independent pass 1 at candidate a8fde8192bea44755d24fcdeede5ea32da30a26e (HEAD matched), read the full base-to-candidate diff and touched files/tests, and made no edits; per-criterion verdicts:
- AC-3 NOT SATISFIED: src/math.mjs:72 returns 3 for [3,1,2] and 1 for [5], instead of 2 and 0;
- R-1 SATISFIED for validation behavior: src/math.mjs:69-71 rejects non-arrays and invalid elements with TypeError and empty arrays with RangeError, independently probed;
- R-2 SATISFIED for implementation behavior: src/math.mjs:69-72 only reads input, independently probed;
- R-3 SATISFIED: full diff preserves existing functions (src/math.mjs:1-66) and existing test cases (test/math.test.mjs:5-83), changing only the permitted existing import at test/math.test.mjs:3;
- R-4 SATISFIED: full diff changes only src/math.mjs and test/math.test.mjs, adds no dependencies, and leaves generated files unchanged;
- R-5 SATISFIED: the new test at test/math.test.mjs:85 uses the range prefix and is isolated by the required command.
Findings:
- HIGH | src/math.mjs:72 and test/math.test.mjs:86 | Extra +1 violates max-minus-min and the test asserts the incorrect result, allowing broken behavior to pass | Verify range([3,1,2]) === 2 and range([5]) === 0 with corrected candidate tests;
- MEDIUM | src/math.mjs:72 | Spreading all elements into Math.max/min throws RangeError for a valid million-element plain array, imposing an unspecified argument-count limit | Verify range(Array(1000000).fill(5)) === 0 without throwing;
- MEDIUM | test/math.test.mjs:85 | No singleton test exercises the explicitly required singleton rule, leaving the observed singleton defect undetected | Add a range-prefixed assertion that range([5]) === 0;
- MEDIUM | test/math.test.mjs:85 | No range test exercises non-array rejection, leaving R-1 shape validation unprotected | Add a range-prefixed TypeError assertion for non-array input;
- MEDIUM | test/math.test.mjs:85 | No range test exercises empty-array rejection, leaving R-1 empty-input validation unprotected | Add a range-prefixed RangeError assertion for [];
- MEDIUM | test/math.test.mjs:85 | No range test exercises invalid/non-finite element rejection, leaving R-1 element validation unprotected | Add range-prefixed TypeError assertions for a non-number and NaN/Infinity;
- MEDIUM | test/math.test.mjs:85 | No range test exercises input preservation, leaving R-2 unprotected | Add a range-prefixed test comparing an unsorted input with its original contents after the call.
Checks run: node --test --test-name-pattern="^range" test/ exited 0 with "tests 1", "pass 1", "fail 0"; npm test exited 1 with "tests 16", "pass 15", "fail 1" and only "clamp respects upper bound" failing (unchanged and excluded); independent node -e probes printed "range([3,1,2]) = 3; expected 2", "range([5]) = 1; expected 0", PASS for shape/empty/element validation and input preservation, and "FAIL: valid million-element array throws RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded"; the initial heredoc probe could not run because the read-only sandbox denied its temporary file, then the same probes ran without file writes using -e; git status --short was empty; remaining uncertainty: no unavailable required checks, candidate tests still need repair and rerunning, and acceptance remains the coordinator's decision.
